        "note": "The version of the formalization cited by the paper (Lean v4.31.0, Mathlib fabf563a).  The Lean package lean/ of the submitted commit is that of tag v1.1.0 (commit 23dabdf6...), which ports it to Lean v4.35.0, Mathlib v4.35.0 and the Lean module system, which Palomar requires.  Port summary: every file is a `module` with `public import`s and an `@[expose] public section`; 13 private helpers were made public (names unchanged); no declaration was renamed or deleted and no statement was edited; Mathlib's change of `CategoryTheory.Aut X` from `X ≅ X` to a one-field structure is absorbed by accessor abbreviations `RQuiver.Aut.hom/inv`; the Galois action on L ⊗_K V is now Mathlib's `TensorProduct.leftDistribMulAction` (same name and type); 523 declarations (or sections) carry `set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false`, an elaborator unification setting restoring the pre-v4.3x behaviour for types (it affects elaboration only; the kernel check is unaffected).  The port's own audit: 0 sorry and only propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound over all 11638 declarations; the 109 formalized statements of the paper's appendix have the same types as in v1.0.0 under the default printer (with explicit printing they differ only in Mathlib's instance paths and three Mathlib renames).",
